# Array.from([1]), where the library's from goes over `items` with for-of
# The code behind Array.from (runtimefunction 48) is entered with operands nobody knows and goes over one of them. That a call of Array.from goes over its operand the records say where the call is:
# there the array is opened and stepped. Here nothing is opened and nothing is stepped, so no method nobody knows is called: no code that nobody compiles writes anything. A step answers a value nobody knows.
# Without records: going-over-an-unknown-operand-in-library-code-that-no-record-describes-is-unknown-code.ir
